# Top-level pins for the Python binding jobs: python.yml, ci.yml test-python,
# nightly.yml and bench_baremetal.yml.
#
# One file serves every Python and OS those jobs run on. Compile it on the
# OLDEST Python in the python.yml matrix (3.8), the one whose dependency set is
# the widest: pytest 9 needs Python 3.10+, so pytest is pinned to the last
# series that supports 3.8, and the resolved set (exceptiongroup, tomli,
# typing-extensions) is a superset of what 3.10 and 3.12 need. pytest asks for
# colorama on Windows only, and pip-compile drops a requirement whose marker is
# false on the machine that compiles, so a macOS or Linux compile would omit it
# and the Windows install would fail under --require-hashes. It is therefore
# listed unconditionally: a pure-Python wheel that is harmless elsewhere.
#
# Refresh recipe: docs/CI.md, "Hashed Python requirements".
maturin==1.15.0
pytest==8.3.5
colorama==0.4.6
